 or television appearances are restricted. The NCAA's probationary period and sanctions will run concurrently with the conference's penalty, which reduced grants-in-aid for men's basketball from 15 to 13 for the 1983-84 academic year. The NCAA's Committee on Infractions found that the punitive and corrective actions already taken by the Pacific Coast Athletic Association and the university were sufficient, but individual sanctions were imposed against the head football coach and one assistant coach due to their awareness of the violations. The NCAA's Division I institutions must now conduct their regular-season competition under eligibility rules at least as stringent as those applicable to Division I members. Division II institutions must remain in compliance with Bylaws I I-2-(a), (b), (d), and (e). The new Arena I system, which has been installed in three Major League Baseball parks, can be adapted for college football stadiums and basketball arenas, providing broadcasters with a cohesive system and reducing the need for costly surveys and setups. The system costs approximately $72,000 to $77,000 to install in a basketball arena, with a projected third of that cost for a football stadium.", key_facts=['California State University, Fresno, placed on probation until June 1, 1984', 'Head football coach and one assistant coach prohibited from off-campus recruiting until August 1, 1984', 'No postseason competition or television appearances restricted', "NCAA's probationary period and sanctions will run concurrently with the conference's penalty", "NCAA's Division I institutions must conduct regular-season competition under eligibility rules at least as stringent as those applicable to Division I members", "NCAA's Division II institutions must remain in compliance with Bylaws I I-2-(a), (b), (d), and (e)", "NCAA's Committee on Infractions found that the punitive and corrective actions already taken by the Pacific Coast Athletic Association and the university were suffi