all hours vary from 11 a.m. to 10 p.m. daily, with specific hours for luxury stores and attractions. Parking is free for the first 15 minutes, then $5 plus tax thereafter.", key_facts=[]), BatchSummary(summary='American Dream is a mixed retail and entertainment destination in East Rutherford, New Jersey. It combines approximately 450 retail units with a Nickelodeon Universe indoor theme park, a DreamWorks indoor water park, Sea Life Aquarium, and LEGOLAND Discovery Center within a single structure. Located 10 km west of Midtown Manhattan, it attracts visitors from affluent Bergen County suburbs and urban markets. The center features luxury and contemporary fashion retail, with luxury anchors including Balenciaga, Dolce and Gabbana, Gucci, Hermes, and Piaget. Entertainment anchors include Nickelodeon Universe, indoor water park, Sea Life, and LEGOLAND Discovery Center. The center is accessible via NJ Transit bus routes and NJ Transit station. It serves a catchment area including northern New Jersey residents and tourists from the New York tri-state area. The entertainment component generates a regional tourist catchment extending the property’s effective draw zone to a 2-hour drive radius, independent of purely retail-motivated trips. The center has a unique position in the New York metropolitan retail map as the only major retail development combining luxury and mainstream fashion retail with large-scale indoor entertainment at theme park scale, insulating against pure retail traffic patterns and generating repeat visitation driven by attractions like the water park and theme park.', key_facts=[])]
