rs: Eddie Bauer LLC, et al. Case No. 26-11422 (SLM). Claims arising out of the rejection of contracts must be filed on or before the later of (a) the deadline for filing proofs of claim and (b) thirty days after the later to occur of (i) the effective date of such rejection and (ii) the date the Rejection Order is entered. The automatic stay is modified to allow the disposition of such property, free and clear of all liens, claims, and encumbrances, effective as of the Rejection Date. The Debtors are authorized to take all actions necessary to effectuate the relief granted in this Order and the rejection.', key_facts=[]), BatchSummary(summary="American Dream is a large integrated attraction in New Jersey offering shopping, entertainment, and dining. It features renowned brands, multiple theme parks, and diverse dining options. American Dream's management and financial obligations are significant risks due to its project-specific assets and lack of state backing. The PILOT Assignment Agreement and prioritization of PILOT Share payments ensure financial stability for local communities. The property's entertainment anchors, such as the indoor ski slope and water park, generate regional tourist traffic and repeat visitation. Its unique entertainment-anchored model sets it apart from other retail developments in the New York metropolitan area.", key_facts=[])]
